// Who is changing the subscription? Any successful administrative write or delete by a caller
// other than the remediation identity. In this design every change arrives through a reviewed
// pull request and a pipeline apply, so a row is a prompt to match it to a merged change; a row
// with no matching change is an out-of-band change. terraform plan (drift.yml) answers the other
// question: does reality still match the code.
// Rendered by templatefile() in tripwire.tf, which supplies remediation_principal_id.
AzureActivity
| where CategoryValue == "Administrative"
| where ActivityStatusValue in~ ("Success", "Succeeded")
| where OperationNameValue endswith "/write" or OperationNameValue endswith "/delete"
| where isnotempty(Caller)
| where tolower(Caller) != tolower("${remediation_principal_id}")
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, OperationNameValue, ResourceGroup, _ResourceId, CorrelationId
